Q: Duplicate rows CodeIgniter A: <p>Although it is not totally irrelevant but it is very useful to build up your own generic functions or modules that serves your requirements. Here is check_duplicate function working as generic function checking duplicate data entry in DB. Here is the function</p>

<pre><code>function _check_duplicate($table_name,$param)
{
    $row_count=$this-&gt;db-&gt;get_where($table_name,$param)-&gt;num_rows();
    if(count($row_count&gt;0))
    {
        return true;
    }
    else
    {
        return false;
    }
}
</code></pre>

<p>here is how you call the function;</p>

<pre><code>if($this-&gt;_check_duplicate('table_name',array('param1'=&gt;$param1,'param2'=&gt;$param2)))
{
    // redirect to some page
}
else
{
    // do something, insert or update
}
</code></pre>

<p>for parameters, you can pass as many parameters as required. this function can be generic in a controller or can be part of generic module. It depends how you use it.</p>

Q: Getting &#39;psutil.AccessDenied (pid=6836)&#39; error using psutil A: <p>I’m assuming that notepad is running as the user running your script and that you intend to ignore processes running as admin, as that would not include your notepad process.</p>
<p>There may be a better way to deal with errors in a list/dict/generator comprehension, but I’m using <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/8915613/25261014">this answer</a> for this. You need to catch the permission error and, in this case, return the raised exception.</p>
<pre class="lang-python prettyprint-override"><code>def catch(func, *args, handle=lambda e: e, **kwargs):
    try:
        return func(*args, **kwargs)
    except Exception as e:
        return handle(e)

import psutil
if &quot;notepad.exe&quot; in (catch(p.name) for p in psutil.process_iter()):
    print('program is running')
else:
    print('not running')
</code></pre>
